  "caveats": [
    "Pearson dispersion \u03c6 = 21.84, so the quasi-Poisson covariance scaling was applied: every band below is 4.67x wider than a plain-Poisson fit would have reported. The point estimates are unchanged \u2014 scaling touches the covariance only. A \u03c6 this far above 1 means unmodelled heterogeneity, which is expected on real grouped data and is why the scaling is not optional here.",
    "The base offset is estimated from these same cells, so `overall_ae` is ~1 by construction and is not an independent check on the level. The fitted improvement is unaffected: it is a calendar contrast, and every calendar-invariant term \u2014 the offset included \u2014 cancels in the difference."
  ],
